# Fitted footer text

New screens and status lines use the shared footer font. Do not hard-code `setTextSize(1)` for a hint, status, or footer.

- A bottom status line calls `ui::drawFittedFooter(text)` (`src/ui/fitted_text.h`).
- Any other single-line caption that must stay on screen calls `ui::fitTextSize(text, max_width)` before drawing.
- Both start at text size 2 and step down by 0.25 until the string fits the width. Do not copy that loop into an app.

```cpp
// Bottom hint
ui::drawFittedFooter("Enter OK");

// Centered caption
ui::fitTextSize("any key / wait", display.width() - 8);
display.drawString("any key / wait", display.width() / 2, y);
```

List rows, titles, and values stay `setTextSize(2)` unless the string is one of these captions.
